# Loop head merges the states of different breaks

Verifies a break contributes the state it jumped with. The first iteration
rewrites `a[1]` and breaks, so `a[0]` is never written and keeps its millimeter
subtype across the loop, while the rewritten slot is read at runtime.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm, 20mm]

for (i in 0..2) {
    if (i == 0) {
        a[1] = 5cm
        break
    }
    a[0] = 2cm
    break
}

print(a[0] + 1mm)
print(a[1] + 1mm)

<<< stdout
11mm
51mm

<<< stderr
